  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.PostgresqlProperties\": {\n        \"summary\": \"A Spring Boot configuration properties class that holds PostgreSQL database connection settings. Annotated with @ConfigurationProperties(prefix = \\\"postgresql\\\"), it automatically binds configuration properties from application configuration files (e.g., application.properties or application.yml) to its fields. The class contains four essential database connection properties: username (database username), password (database password), driverClass (JDBC driver class name), and url (database connection URL). Each property has standard getter and setter methods, enabling Spring Boot to inject values from externalized configuration with keys like postgresql.username, postgresql.password, postgresql.driverClass, and postgresql.url. This class follows the JavaBean pattern and enables type-safe, externalized configuration management for PostgreSQL database connections.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/PostgresqlProperties.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
